summary: perl module streams resolve against every perl stream
description:
    The perl module family is built once per perl stream, one context each.
    All contexts of a build batch must share a single modulemd version; when
    they do not, dnf cannot resolve the contexts built for the other streams --
    it prints a "Modular dependency problems" block on every transaction while
    still exiting 0, and 'dnf module enable' fails outright.
test: ./test.sh
